# Common Rules

## Naming

| Type | File | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| Controller | `auth_controller.ts` | kebab + `_controller.ts` |
| Validator | `auth_validator.ts` | **must** end with `_validator.ts` |
| Service | `auth_service.ts` | class with `@inject()` |
| Middleware | `auth_middleware.ts` | |
| Vue SFC | `sign-in.vue` | kebab-case files; PascalCase component names |
| shadcn-vue | under `web/src/components/ui/` | |

- Classes/interfaces: `PascalCase`
- Functions/vars: `camelCase`
- Constants: `as const` objects, not TypeScript `enum`

## Style

- 2 spaces, single quotes, ~100 cols, no semicolons, no trailing commas
- Prefer `import type`; avoid `any`; prefer `| null` over `undefined` for optionals

## Constants

Put shared constants in one summary file per package (`app/constants/index.ts` or `web` equivalent). Split only past ~500 lines. Status/type/mode/API literals used ≥2 times must be constants—no scattered magic strings.

## Services vs utils

- **Services**: business logic classes with `@inject()` only
- **Utils**: plain functions/values under `utils/`, never under `services/`

## Quality

Project verification commands (run the smallest relevant set before claiming done):

```bash
pnpm run lint
pnpm run typecheck
pnpm run test   # backend / affected tests
```
